    "invariants": [
      "Native region generation floors chunk coordinates to a region, passes origin=region*32 and side=32, and opts in only when all1024 slots are fresh.",
      "Other paths retain the existing reuse_regions=false contract. Cache also requires registered profile pointer identity, source order, material layers and material halo.",
      "Cache capture filters full normalized context, roots and the existing neighboring region range. Cache insertion replaces same-context/same-region entries, so captured production snapshots are unique and disjoint.",
      "The new neighborhood owns the same Arc snapshots in nine optional positions; no global cap, eviction, publication or cleanup changes. Empty captures return before coordinate conversion.",
      "Region selection uses floor division by512 for negative coordinates and i64 differences to avoid overflow. No entries outside the existing capture neighborhood are required; all misses retain full planner fallback.",
      "The selected archive still applies exact bounds, omitted center, strict before-root and missing-latest behavior.",
      "ChunkRequest validates chunk-to-block checked multiplication before native aligned region generation. The final fixture initializes negative-coordinate interior positions and capture timing includes local index construction."
    ],
    "tests_added": [
      "Direct lookup versus the prior scan over positive/negative source-region edges and holes, comparing exact backing owners.",
      "Empty and extreme-coordinate cases.",
      "Real cache replacement and captured-owner lifetime, including a returned column outliving its snapshot."
